		<description><![CDATA[Darwesh your name was truly well given
Wandering, wisdom with little kept hidden
Double Sagittarian – fire through and through
Nothing could stop you, - did what you had to do.

The ‘Waters of Life’ and the book of the Tao
The work of Abwun all gave you strength some how
You’d travel the world to conferences and meetings
Ever awake - with a heart full of warm greetings.

Your love for your teacher was upright and true
Saadi and his work touched healing in you.
The broad inspiration of Inayat and Sam
Resonated deeply with your truth, “This I am.”

And then, suddenly you were gone …
Still your light ever lingers on
You’ll not be forgotten
The Light of your heart will never be ‘gone’.


Thanks Darwesh Joost for all you were, all you are, and especially for all the Wisdom you shared. Thank you. ZubinNur]]></description>
		<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>Darwesh your name was truly well given<br />
Wandering, wisdom with little kept hidden<br />
Double Sagittarian – fire through and through<br />
Nothing could stop you, &#8211; did what you had to do.</p>
<p>The ‘Waters of Life’ and the book of the Tao<br />
The work of Abwun all gave you strength some how<br />
You’d travel the world to conferences and meetings<br />
Ever awake &#8211; with a heart full of warm greetings.</p>
<p>Your love for your teacher was upright and true<br />
Saadi and his work touched healing in you.<br />
The broad inspiration of Inayat and Sam<br />
Resonated deeply with your truth, “This I am.”</p>
<p>And then, suddenly you were gone …<br />
Still your light ever lingers on<br />
You’ll not be forgotten<br />
The Light of your heart will never be ‘gone’.</p>
<p>Thanks Darwesh Joost for all you were, all you are, and especially for all the Wisdom you shared. Thank you. ZubinNur</p>
